<title>TURKEY: Petrol Ofisi 9-mth profits rise 88 pct.</title>
<headline>Petrol Ofisi 9-mth profits rise 88 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	2,516.52  vs   1,340.39</p>
<p>    Net profit			 6,341.63  vs   3,377.79</p>
<p>    Net sales			209,930.16  vs 111,449.67</p>
<p>    Operating profit		10,841.16  vs   5,598.58</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     5,877.16  vs   3,835.86</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	    4,422.76  vs   2,450.55</p>
<p>    Interest paid			  0     vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts		     21,113.77  vs  10,089.07</p>
<p>    Equity			    12,285.18  vs   7,790.06</p>
<p>    Capital			    2,520.00  vs   2,520.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's largely state owned petroleum products marketer Petrol Ofisi A.S. is slated for privatisation, with 93.3 percent of its capital held by the privatisation agency OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
